WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.376
(paper airplane whooshes)

00:00:03.376 --> 00:00:04.250
- What's up, Believe Nation?
(mellow orchestral music)

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.570
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.723
My one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:07.723 --> 00:00:09.370
that entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.503
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:11.503 --> 00:00:13.422
I started the MentorMe
series with the goal

00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:16.531
to try to learn from people
who have done more than us,

00:00:16.531 --> 00:00:18.625
and by hanging around
them a little bit longer,

00:00:18.625 --> 00:00:20.420
hopefully, some of
their mindsets are added

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.485
to their beliefs, their confidence,

00:00:22.485 --> 00:00:26.710
seep into us to help us become
the best version ourselves.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.722
Today, we're going to
learn from Lisa Nichols.

00:00:28.722 --> 00:00:31.385
and how to live a purpose-driven life.

00:00:31.385 --> 00:00:33.212
As always, guys, as you're watching clips,

00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:35.439
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:37.866
please leave it in quotes
in the comments below.

00:00:37.866 --> 00:00:40.116
You might win a prize, but also,

00:00:40.116 --> 00:00:42.026
when you write it down,
it's much more likely

00:00:42.026 --> 00:00:44.391
to stick with yourself as well.

00:00:44.391 --> 00:00:45.419
Enjoy.

00:00:45.419 --> 00:00:49.086
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.467
- When we talk about living our quest,

00:01:02.793 --> 00:01:05.826
I think that living my quest, really,

00:01:05.826 --> 00:01:07.540
if I look at it on a daily basis,

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.707
it's finding my own voice.

00:01:10.546 --> 00:01:11.950
It's finding your voice.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.700
It's finding the song
that only you can sing,

00:01:17.029 --> 00:01:19.000
off key or not.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.632
It's finding your rhythm.

00:01:21.632 --> 00:01:23.500
It's discovering what it feels like

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.833
to walk in your shoes today.

00:01:27.191 --> 00:01:29.649
It won't look like it looked 10 years ago.

00:01:29.649 --> 00:01:33.649
Living your quest is,
what can I do with my life

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:39.015
so that my life becomes
infectious to someone else?

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:41.059
Living my quest looks like,

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:44.559
how do I make my fingerprint matter so big

00:01:45.506 --> 00:01:48.707
that it lives beyond my transition day?

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:52.600
Living your quest is, how can I forgive

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.524
the perceivingly unforgivable

00:01:55.524 --> 00:01:58.441
so I can love the absolute lovable?

00:01:59.415 --> 00:02:03.336
Living your quest is, how do I give myself

00:02:03.336 --> 00:02:06.262
1,000 second chances, and every time

00:02:06.262 --> 00:02:09.208
I get to 999, press reset?

00:02:09.208 --> 00:02:10.700
(audience laughs)

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.617
Yeah? Yeah.

00:02:13.892 --> 00:02:16.188
Living my quest is not some

00:02:16.188 --> 00:02:19.021
ambiguous, untouchable experience.

00:02:20.141 --> 00:02:22.811
Living my quest means going back

00:02:22.811 --> 00:02:25.371
and healing the little girl in me

00:02:25.371 --> 00:02:27.679
so that the woman can be free.

00:02:27.679 --> 00:02:30.684
It's going back and embracing
the little boy in you

00:02:30.684 --> 00:02:32.697
so that the man can show up

00:02:32.697 --> 00:02:35.916
and give himself permission
to cry when necessary.

00:02:35.916 --> 00:02:39.980
Living your quest is not
something that you can't touch.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.768
It's not something that requires a stage,

00:02:41.768 --> 00:02:43.291
or lights, or cameras.

00:02:43.291 --> 00:02:46.045
Living your quest is
being complete and content

00:02:46.045 --> 00:02:48.890
with who you are in the dark of the night

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:52.364
so who you are in the middle
of the day is all right.

00:02:52.364 --> 00:02:57.085
Living your quest is as
simple as it is complex.

00:02:57.085 --> 00:03:00.146
Living your quest is about
giving yourself permission,

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.272
say, "permission."

00:03:01.272 --> 00:03:02.360
- [Audience] Permission.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.718
- On a daily basis to become

00:03:04.718 --> 00:03:07.704
the next best version of yourself.

00:03:07.704 --> 00:03:10.061
Living your quest is not holding yourself

00:03:10.061 --> 00:03:12.241
hostage to old decisions,

00:03:12.241 --> 00:03:15.025
not holding yourself
hostage to shame, blame,

00:03:15.025 --> 00:03:16.825
guilt, regret, and anger.

00:03:16.825 --> 00:03:19.082
Living your quest is about recognizing

00:03:19.082 --> 00:03:23.378
that every day, I can be
reborn to my possibility.

00:03:23.378 --> 00:03:27.627
See, living your quest is
as internal and personal

00:03:27.627 --> 00:03:29.365
as it is public.

00:03:29.365 --> 00:03:32.148
Living your quest is about recognizing

00:03:32.148 --> 00:03:34.018
that you have brilliance in you,

00:03:34.018 --> 00:03:37.887
and not being willing to
dim your light one more day.

00:03:37.887 --> 00:03:40.499
Living your quest means not being afraid

00:03:40.499 --> 00:03:43.332
of the genius in you, even
though you have doubt.

00:03:43.332 --> 00:03:45.516
Living your quest is recognizing that

00:03:45.516 --> 00:03:48.220
you get to sing your song off tune,

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.211
that you get to live in perfection

00:03:50.211 --> 00:03:52.832
while you master imperfection.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.014
Myth number two is that abundance

00:03:55.014 --> 00:03:58.931
is singularly focused on
possessions and money.

00:03:59.789 --> 00:04:02.389
Right? It's all about what you drive,

00:04:02.389 --> 00:04:04.564
what you live in, how much money you make,

00:04:04.564 --> 00:04:08.708
when in fact, this couldn't
be further from the truth.

00:04:08.708 --> 00:04:11.910
Wealth is possessions and money.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:14.410
Abundance is a 360 experience.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.139
Write it down.

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:19.639
Abundance is a 360 experience.

00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:25.726
True abundance, true
abundance is your health,

00:04:25.726 --> 00:04:27.177
'cause if you don't have great health,

00:04:27.177 --> 00:04:29.505
life does not feel good.

00:04:29.505 --> 00:04:31.727
Abundance is relationship.

00:04:31.727 --> 00:04:33.446
At the end of your life, literally,

00:04:33.446 --> 00:04:35.925
you will measure the quality of your life

00:04:35.925 --> 00:04:39.228
by the quality of the
relationships you had.

00:04:39.228 --> 00:04:40.232
All the other stuff will fall away.

00:04:40.232 --> 00:04:41.491
That promotion you're thinking about,

00:04:41.491 --> 00:04:42.772
you're wondering about that raise,

00:04:42.772 --> 00:04:44.824
it will fall away in
the area of importance

00:04:44.824 --> 00:04:45.994
when you get to the end of your life.

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:48.046
You will begin to look at the
quality of your relationships,

00:04:48.046 --> 00:04:49.489
how your children related to you,

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.798
how your siblings related to you,

00:04:50.798 --> 00:04:51.915
do you have love in your life.

00:04:51.915 --> 00:04:54.373
You literally will start
looking at relationships

00:04:54.373 --> 00:04:57.959
at a higher level as you get older.

00:04:57.959 --> 00:05:00.630
When you mind them now,
you take care of them,

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:01.760
and I know that for a fact.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:05.702
I have a friend who's worth $14 billion,

00:05:05.702 --> 00:05:07.002
billion with a B.

00:05:07.002 --> 00:05:09.286
He was just partying at
my house all night long.

00:05:09.286 --> 00:05:12.915
Lee, four in the morning, go home.

00:05:12.915 --> 00:05:15.666
He flew in from Canada to
go to my New Years party

00:05:15.666 --> 00:05:18.400
because he loves my family connection,

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.912
and he doesn't have one.

00:05:19.912 --> 00:05:21.619
He is financially wealthy.

00:05:21.619 --> 00:05:23.813
He's relationship broke.

00:05:23.813 --> 00:05:24.992
Does that make sense?

00:05:24.992 --> 00:05:27.543
Abundance is a 360 experience.

00:05:27.543 --> 00:05:29.926
It's about relationships,
it's about health,

00:05:29.926 --> 00:05:31.676
it's about your spiritual groundedness.

00:05:31.676 --> 00:05:33.577
That doesn't mean you
have a religious origin.

00:05:33.577 --> 00:05:34.898
It's about, can you release?

00:05:34.898 --> 00:05:36.036
Can you forgive?

00:05:36.036 --> 00:05:37.161
Can you let go?

00:05:37.161 --> 00:05:38.257
Can you be still?

00:05:38.257 --> 00:05:40.381
Do you meditate, do you
have time with yourself?

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:41.327
That has a lot to do

00:05:41.327 --> 00:05:44.912
with the quality of
your life, that ability.

00:05:44.912 --> 00:05:48.924
Visualization is a gift to
your heart and your soul.

00:05:48.924 --> 00:05:52.674
It's a gift because, if
the idea is the seed,

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:57.434
visualization is the fertilizer.

00:05:59.733 --> 00:06:02.791
It's the fertilizer,
because, when your thoughts

00:06:02.791 --> 00:06:04.731
are connected with an emotion,

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.666
see, you would visualize yourself winning,

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:09.083
and you would feel all the
emotion that came with that,

00:06:09.083 --> 00:06:10.810
and all you're doing now is,

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.217
you're not chasing a foreign emotion.

00:06:13.217 --> 00:06:14.894
You know the feeling, and now,

00:06:14.894 --> 00:06:16.093
you're just doing what's necessary

00:06:16.093 --> 00:06:19.384
to get back to that feeling in real time.

00:06:19.384 --> 00:06:21.976
What a good friend of mine, Vishen,

00:06:21.976 --> 00:06:24.526
the CEO of Mindvalley, who you know,

00:06:24.526 --> 00:06:27.482
I did a visualization
with him, we were in Bali,

00:06:27.482 --> 00:06:32.112
and he said to me afterwards,
"I never get emotional.

00:06:32.112 --> 00:06:33.040
"I cried."
- He doesn't.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:33.955
He doesn't get emotional.

00:06:33.955 --> 00:06:36.340
He's, like, super, yeah.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:38.718
- He was like, "I cried, I got emotional."

00:06:38.718 --> 00:06:40.968
He goes, "I figured it out.

00:06:42.149 --> 00:06:45.210
"A good visualization brings in emotion."

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.740
He was like, "That's how you do it."

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.411
I love doing visualizations,

00:06:50.411 --> 00:06:52.312
and it's real important,
in the visualization,

00:06:52.312 --> 00:06:54.048
you can't see it over there.

00:06:54.048 --> 00:06:55.604
You have to see it right here.

00:06:55.604 --> 00:06:57.148
- To feel it.
- You got to feel it

00:06:57.148 --> 00:07:00.021
right here, like, it's all I am.

00:07:00.021 --> 00:07:01.130
I am.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.140
I am in my dream home.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.264
I am in my dream relationship,

00:07:05.264 --> 00:07:07.081
and then unpack what that looks like,

00:07:07.081 --> 00:07:09.684
but most importantly,
unpack what it feels like.

00:07:09.684 --> 00:07:13.281
When you have that emotion in this moment,

00:07:13.281 --> 00:07:15.040
all of a sudden, you stir up something

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.236
that I don't think will
ever go back to sleep.

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.685
It'll go, "Okay, let's go get that."

00:07:18.685 --> 00:07:20.809
What it really does is, it sets up a state

00:07:20.809 --> 00:07:24.387
of cognitive dissonance,
and cognitive dissonance

00:07:24.387 --> 00:07:26.663
is when you see something in your mind,

00:07:26.663 --> 00:07:28.207
and you see yourself in a way

00:07:28.207 --> 00:07:31.295
that your behaviors are
not currently leading to,

00:07:31.295 --> 00:07:33.905
so your mind becomes
disrupted, and it goes,

00:07:33.905 --> 00:07:35.459
"Okay, can we get there?"

00:07:35.459 --> 00:07:36.618
- Right, 'cause I'm not there right now.

00:07:36.618 --> 00:07:38.499
- I'm not there right now,
and that's not comfortable.

00:07:38.499 --> 00:07:40.661
Your mind wants to literally be congruent,

00:07:40.661 --> 00:07:41.953
what it thinks is what you're doing,

00:07:41.953 --> 00:07:43.851
what it thinks is what you're doing.

00:07:43.851 --> 00:07:45.529
When you set up a constant,

00:07:45.529 --> 00:07:47.204
and abundant thinkers like you and I,

00:07:47.204 --> 00:07:51.186
we do it unconsciously, we
are constantly keeping ourself

00:07:51.186 --> 00:07:53.703
in a state of cognitive dissonance,

00:07:53.703 --> 00:07:55.667
meaning, okay, what else?

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:57.618
I'm seeing Lisa over there, and I'm going,

00:07:57.618 --> 00:08:01.785
"Okay, let me go," while
being grateful for my now.

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.237
It's not in that I'm going
to be whole and complete

00:08:05.237 --> 00:08:06.354
when I get over there.

00:08:06.354 --> 00:08:08.020
I'm whole and complete now.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.492
I just know I'm supposed to be over there,

00:08:09.492 --> 00:08:11.483
so let me do what's
necessary to get over there,

00:08:11.483 --> 00:08:14.583
and let me evict any
behaviors or characteristics

00:08:14.583 --> 00:08:16.257
that are stopping me, and let me adopt

00:08:16.257 --> 00:08:18.077
any new ones that I need.

00:08:18.077 --> 00:08:19.235
You're super achievers.

00:08:19.235 --> 00:08:20.617
I'm a super achiever.

00:08:20.617 --> 00:08:23.055
One thing we have to
constantly remind ourself

00:08:23.055 --> 00:08:27.138
is to create micro wins
to get to our macro wins,

00:08:28.602 --> 00:08:30.235
that we go after the macro win,

00:08:30.235 --> 00:08:31.943
but we only look at the macro win.

00:08:31.943 --> 00:08:33.954
I want you to look at the micro wins

00:08:33.954 --> 00:08:36.738
and get five micro wins under your belt

00:08:36.738 --> 00:08:39.277
so you can create your macro win.

00:08:39.277 --> 00:08:43.373
That way, you celebrate
yourself a lot more often,

00:08:43.373 --> 00:08:44.206
yes, yes?

00:08:45.199 --> 00:08:46.989
That way, you can have an indicator

00:08:46.989 --> 00:08:49.001
that you're on the right track more often.

00:08:49.001 --> 00:08:52.138
That way, your fuel is being
acknowledged more often.

00:08:52.138 --> 00:08:54.060
That way, you know you're
on the right track.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:57.441
Let's get to micro wins, micro wins,

00:08:57.441 --> 00:08:59.789
micro wins can lead to a macro win.

00:08:59.789 --> 00:09:00.866
Can we agree with that?

00:09:00.866 --> 00:09:04.620
I'm showing you how
abundant thinkers think.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.279
To me, you model successful people.

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:07.915
When I was on the Oprah Winfrey show,

00:09:07.915 --> 00:09:09.367
on one of the commercial breaks, she said,

00:09:09.367 --> 00:09:11.959
"So Lisa, how many coaches do you have?"

00:09:11.959 --> 00:09:15.068
She didn't ask me if I had a coach.

00:09:15.068 --> 00:09:16.386
She said, "How many coaches do you have?"

00:09:16.386 --> 00:09:17.553
I said, "Two."

00:09:19.134 --> 00:09:22.858
On the next commercial
break, what you think I did?

00:09:22.858 --> 00:09:26.921
I asked her, "How many
coaches do you have?"

00:09:26.921 --> 00:09:28.338
She said, "Four."

00:09:29.412 --> 00:09:31.261
When I left the show,
what do you think I did?

00:09:31.261 --> 00:09:32.286
(audience laughs)

00:09:32.286 --> 00:09:33.232
Right?

00:09:33.232 --> 00:09:35.792
I hired two more coaches.

00:09:35.792 --> 00:09:37.263
Success leaves clues.

00:09:37.263 --> 00:09:39.449
I'm going to give you some of the clues.

00:09:39.449 --> 00:09:41.865
People who are living
an abundant life now,

00:09:41.865 --> 00:09:45.715
you guys just allow this to
be a salve of confirmation.

00:09:45.715 --> 00:09:47.930
Then, for everyone else who's
moving in that direction

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:49.576
and moreso in that direction,

00:09:49.576 --> 00:09:52.592
these are the things that
abundant-thinking people do

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:53.761
all day every day.

00:09:53.761 --> 00:09:57.378
One, we create micro wins
so we can get to macro wins,

00:09:57.378 --> 00:10:00.234
and we celebrate the micro wins.

00:10:00.234 --> 00:10:02.376
Far more celebrations in life.

00:10:02.376 --> 00:10:05.252
You are only going to go as
far as you think you're worthy.

00:10:05.252 --> 00:10:06.581
I can push, you can push.

00:10:06.581 --> 00:10:08.410
You can have the greatest product,

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.136
but if you don't feel
worthy, you will work hard

00:10:10.136 --> 00:10:12.609
to sabotage that relationship.

00:10:12.609 --> 00:10:13.817
- Every day, you will.

00:10:13.817 --> 00:10:14.972
- Right, you don't know you're doing it.

00:10:14.972 --> 00:10:16.620
You just think, "These
are the things I need,"

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.458
and you're driving that guy away.

00:10:18.458 --> 00:10:19.932
You're driving that woman away

00:10:19.932 --> 00:10:21.322
because your self-worth says

00:10:21.322 --> 00:10:23.192
they weren't going to stay forever anyway,

00:10:23.192 --> 00:10:25.641
or self-worth around money.

00:10:25.641 --> 00:10:27.255
You have a cap that you feel like

00:10:27.255 --> 00:10:28.879
you're worthy of a million dollars,

00:10:28.879 --> 00:10:33.289
you will always get to
999,000, and you will stop

00:10:33.289 --> 00:10:34.508
because your self-worth says it.

00:10:34.508 --> 00:10:37.719
- What's a good exercise or
process that we can follow

00:10:37.719 --> 00:10:40.195
on a daily basis, maybe something simple,

00:10:40.195 --> 00:10:42.769
to enhance our enrichment and worthiness?

00:10:42.769 --> 00:10:43.712
- Absolutely.

00:10:43.712 --> 00:10:46.394
I did this for six months every single day

00:10:46.394 --> 00:10:49.198
right after I brushed my teeth.

00:10:49.198 --> 00:10:51.555
It's the I See You exercise.

00:10:51.555 --> 00:10:52.388
You get in the mirror.

00:10:52.388 --> 00:10:55.821
Now, it's not necessarily simple

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:57.248
'cause you dealing with yourself,

00:10:57.248 --> 00:10:59.562
and as complicated as you
are will be the degree.

00:10:59.562 --> 00:11:00.499
- The mechanics of it are simple.

00:11:00.499 --> 00:11:02.707
- Right, the mechanics
are very simple, yes.

00:11:02.707 --> 00:11:04.443
I appreciate that distinction.

00:11:04.443 --> 00:11:05.276
You get in the mirror,

00:11:05.276 --> 00:11:06.424
you complete three different sentences.

00:11:06.424 --> 00:11:08.171
You want to write this down.

00:11:08.171 --> 00:11:10.133
The first sentence, you look at yourself,

00:11:10.133 --> 00:11:12.023
and you say your name, so
you would say, "Louis,"

00:11:12.023 --> 00:11:14.348
and you complete the sentence,
"I'm proud that you,"

00:11:14.348 --> 00:11:17.251
and find seven different things every day

00:11:17.251 --> 00:11:19.506
to celebrate yourself
four, seven different.

00:11:19.506 --> 00:11:21.633
Each day, you can do the same
thing you did the day before,

00:11:21.633 --> 00:11:24.010
but each day, do seven
different things to be proud of.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.579
The second sentence is going
to knock you down a little bit.

00:11:26.579 --> 00:11:29.789
It's going to come from your gut.

00:11:29.789 --> 00:11:33.356
"Louis, I forgive you
for," and cut the shackles

00:11:33.356 --> 00:11:36.900
to blame, shame, guilt, regret, and anger.

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.236
In that sentence, you
cut those five shackles,

00:11:39.236 --> 00:11:41.085
not the first day,
maybe not the third day,

00:11:41.085 --> 00:11:43.901
but by the 21st day, by the 13th day,

00:11:43.901 --> 00:11:45.330
you'll feel some relief.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.934
"Louis, I forgive you for,"

00:11:46.934 --> 00:11:50.086
and go back five years,
15 years, 20 years,

00:11:50.086 --> 00:11:51.732
do that "I forgive you" for that thing

00:11:51.732 --> 00:11:53.369
don't nobody know about but you,

00:11:53.369 --> 00:11:54.709
go ahead and cut those shackles

00:11:54.709 --> 00:11:55.876
'cause if you can still think about it,

00:11:55.876 --> 00:11:57.981
it's still in your energy space.

00:11:57.981 --> 00:12:01.728
The third sentence is,
"Louis, I commit to you that."

00:12:01.728 --> 00:12:02.966
Before you make a commitment

00:12:02.966 --> 00:12:04.775
to anybody else throughout your day,

00:12:04.775 --> 00:12:06.677
you make seven commitments to you.

00:12:06.677 --> 00:12:08.322
The first sentence is,
"I'm proud that you,"

00:12:08.322 --> 00:12:10.282
you're celebrating yourself first.

00:12:10.282 --> 00:12:12.934
We are undercelebrated as a society.

00:12:12.934 --> 00:12:15.052
We look for acknowledgement.

00:12:15.052 --> 00:12:17.091
They interviewed 100 executives

00:12:17.091 --> 00:12:19.294
that all made over a
quarter of a million dollars

00:12:19.294 --> 00:12:21.791
and said, "Would you like a
five percent raise next year,

00:12:21.791 --> 00:12:24.080
"or would you rather be
told thank you more often?"

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:27.707
100%, 100% said, "Keep your money.

00:12:27.707 --> 00:12:29.324
"I'd rather hear thank you."

00:12:29.324 --> 00:12:31.870
We're undercelebrated,
but first, celebrate you.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:32.757
Be the example.

00:12:32.757 --> 00:12:34.728
When I was on Oprah, and
she said, "What do you do?"

00:12:34.728 --> 00:12:36.789
I said, "I recognize that I'm the example

00:12:36.789 --> 00:12:38.800
"of how the rest of the world
is supposed to treat me,

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.314
"and it's my job to give the world

00:12:40.314 --> 00:12:43.081
"the best example of how
I like to be treated."

00:12:43.081 --> 00:12:46.145
Celebrate yourself, forgive
yourself, cut the shackles,

00:12:46.145 --> 00:12:47.682
and then commit to yourself

00:12:47.682 --> 00:12:48.861
before you commit to anyone else.

00:12:48.861 --> 00:12:50.100
That right there.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:50.933
- [Louis] Powerful.

00:12:50.933 --> 00:12:53.178
- That right there will
begin to fill your cup up

00:12:53.178 --> 00:12:54.479
to get to your salsa.

00:12:54.479 --> 00:12:57.871
When you talk about
making your dash dance,

00:12:57.871 --> 00:13:01.871
point one, you got to be
willing to do it afraid.

00:13:03.976 --> 00:13:06.731
See, you might be waiting
for the fear to stop.

00:13:06.731 --> 00:13:07.846
"Lisa," I heard this so many times,

00:13:07.846 --> 00:13:10.550
"Lisa, I'm afraid, what do I do?"

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:12.275
Do it anyway.

00:13:12.275 --> 00:13:13.505
"Lisa, I'm afraid.

00:13:13.505 --> 00:13:15.630
"I don't quite know if I should move."

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.223
Move anyway.

00:13:17.223 --> 00:13:19.416
"I don't know if I should leap."

00:13:19.416 --> 00:13:20.416
Leap afraid,

00:13:22.709 --> 00:13:26.459
and then gather your
courage on the way down.

00:13:27.394 --> 00:13:28.702
If you don't get it before you hit,

00:13:28.702 --> 00:13:31.254
you was going to hit anyway.

00:13:31.254 --> 00:13:34.127
I'd rather die leaping than on the edge

00:13:34.127 --> 00:13:36.868
figuring out how to get the
courage to leap, yes, yes?

00:13:36.868 --> 00:13:37.701
(audience shouts)

00:13:37.701 --> 00:13:38.534
Yes, yes?

00:13:38.534 --> 00:13:39.490
- [Audience] Yes, yes.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:41.819
- So many times, we're waiting.

00:13:41.819 --> 00:13:43.432
We're waiting, I'm waiting.

00:13:43.432 --> 00:13:44.480
I'm waiting to get something right.

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:45.638
I see your hands going up.

00:13:45.638 --> 00:13:48.026
You guys know, if it's your
truth, you can raise your hand

00:13:48.026 --> 00:13:49.537
just like we did on day zero.

00:13:49.537 --> 00:13:50.758
You just kind of waiting.

00:13:50.758 --> 00:13:52.781
You waiting to get everything in order.

00:13:52.781 --> 00:13:54.752
You're waiting, you're waiting so that

00:13:54.752 --> 00:13:56.974
everything is in you, it's together.

00:13:56.974 --> 00:13:58.824
You're waiting to not be afraid.

00:13:58.824 --> 00:14:00.792
You're waiting to have the courage.

00:14:00.792 --> 00:14:02.380
You're waiting to have all the money.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:05.675
You're waiting to lose weight.

00:14:05.675 --> 00:14:07.241
(audience shouts)

00:14:07.241 --> 00:14:10.537
See, if I waited to
release my unwanted pounds

00:14:10.537 --> 00:14:11.933
before I got in front of you,

00:14:11.933 --> 00:14:14.899
Lisa Nichols would be the secret.

00:14:14.899 --> 00:14:17.358
(audience laughs)

00:14:17.358 --> 00:14:18.191
Yes, yes?

00:14:18.191 --> 00:14:19.044
- [Audience] Yes, yes.

00:14:19.044 --> 00:14:23.310
- I thought, "How about I just
leap with my imperfection,

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:27.496
"and then find my form of
perfecting my imperfection

00:14:27.496 --> 00:14:29.232
"while I'm soaring?

00:14:29.232 --> 00:14:31.866
"How about I do that?"

00:14:31.866 --> 00:14:34.761
How about you not wait to get it right?

00:14:34.761 --> 00:14:37.773
You figure out, how does
it look doing it wrong?

00:14:37.773 --> 00:14:39.094
How does that look?

00:14:39.094 --> 00:14:41.643
Your 80% of right is somebody else's

00:14:41.643 --> 00:14:44.436
159% of what they needed.

00:14:44.436 --> 00:14:45.269
Yes, yes?

00:14:45.269 --> 00:14:46.102
- [Audience] Yes, yes.

00:14:46.102 --> 00:14:47.230
- When you want to do it right,

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:48.612
and you want to wait
'til you're not afraid,

00:14:48.612 --> 00:14:50.237
and you want to wait 'til
you have it all together,

00:14:50.237 --> 00:14:52.904
oh, you made it about you again.

00:14:54.138 --> 00:14:55.845
See, Nelson Mandela did it.

00:14:55.845 --> 00:14:57.705
He just did it not
knowing if it were right.

00:14:57.705 --> 00:15:00.741
Mahatma Gandhi just did it
not knowing if it were right.

00:15:00.741 --> 00:15:01.850
Mother Theresa just did it

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:06.178
not looking for affirmation or
confirmation, is this right?

00:15:06.178 --> 00:15:08.074
Martin Luther King did it not even knowing

00:15:08.074 --> 00:15:11.684
if it would happen before his life ended.

00:15:11.684 --> 00:15:13.431
I mean, what are you waiting on?

00:15:13.431 --> 00:15:16.194
Are you willing to do it afraid?

00:15:16.194 --> 00:15:18.072
Are you willing to do it knowing

00:15:18.072 --> 00:15:20.591
that you got so much work
to do to get it better,

00:15:20.591 --> 00:15:22.289
to get it more perfect,
but are you willing

00:15:22.289 --> 00:15:24.016
to do it inside your imperfection?

00:15:24.016 --> 00:15:25.763
Do you realize that, in your imperfection,

00:15:25.763 --> 00:15:27.368
you're perfect for the job?

00:15:27.368 --> 00:15:28.538
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:28.538 --> 00:15:30.245
I'd love to know, what did you think?

00:15:30.245 --> 00:15:31.391
What did you take from this video

00:15:31.391 --> 00:15:33.699
that you're going to
immediately apply somehow

00:15:33.699 --> 00:15:35.597
to your life or to your business?

00:15:35.597 --> 00:15:37.193
Let me know down in the comments below.

00:15:37.193 --> 00:15:38.676
I'm really curious to find out.

00:15:38.676 --> 00:15:41.428
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Melissa Alexandria.

00:15:41.428 --> 00:15:42.992
Melissa, thank you so much for picking up

00:15:42.992 --> 00:15:44.862
a copy of my book, Your One Word,

00:15:44.862 --> 00:15:46.986
and doing that awesome review

00:15:46.986 --> 00:15:48.864
on your YouTube channel around it.

00:15:48.864 --> 00:15:50.348
I really appreciate the support,

00:15:50.348 --> 00:15:52.500
and I'm so glad that
you enjoyed the reading.

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.465
- In this video, I'm
going to be going over

00:15:54.465 --> 00:15:57.641
the book Your One Word by Evan Carmichael.

00:15:57.641 --> 00:16:00.059
This is a book that I
really, really enjoyed.

00:16:00.059 --> 00:16:00.892
- Thank you guys
(mellow orchestral music)

00:16:00.892 --> 00:16:01.910
so much for watching.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:03.040
I believe in you.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.926
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:16:04.926 --> 00:16:08.383
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:16:08.383 --> 00:16:09.883
I'll see you soon.

